WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.105 --> 00:00:04.270
Dácil and the Return of Magec

2
00:00:04.865 --> 00:00:10.225
When the Guanches lived among ravines and
valleys, Dácil looked after goats near

3
00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:15.405
Echeyde. Each dawn she waited for the
first ray of Magec, the Sun, before

4
00:00:15.405 --> 00:00:16.405
setting out.

5
00:00:17.145 --> 00:00:20.050
But one morning, the light did not come.

6
00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:25.450
A black cloud covered the mountain, and
the ground shook beneath their feet.

7
00:00:26.285 --> 00:00:30.865
The elders remembered the story of
Guayota, the being who lived inside the

8
00:00:30.865 --> 00:00:37.025
volcano. According to tradition, he had
captured Magec and was keeping him hidden

9
00:00:37.025 --> 00:00:38.190
in the darkness.

10
00:00:39.365 --> 00:00:41.290
The cold crept into the caves.

11
00:00:42.025 --> 00:00:47.350
Dácil gathered the children beside the
fire, and they all repeated: “Achamán,

12
00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:51.010
bring back Magec and bring back the
light.”

13
00:00:52.145 --> 00:00:54.370
A deep rumbling came from the summit.

14
00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:59.970
The clouds turned red, and a great stone
rolled down to the mouth of Echeyde.

15
00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:06.945
Dácil held her little brother close while
the people of the village called for help

16
00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:09.070
from Achamán, lord of the sky.

17
00:01:10.005 --> 00:01:16.905
Tradition tells us that Achamán came down
from above, defeated Guayota and freed

18
00:01:16.905 --> 00:01:24.125
Magec. Then he sealed the entrance to the
volcano with an enormous rock so that the

19
00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:25.865
being of fire could not escape.

20
00:01:25.865 --> 00:01:30.370
Then a golden line appeared behind
Echeyde.

21
00:01:31.245 --> 00:01:39.230
First it lit up the summit, then the
slopes and, last of all, Dácil’s face.

22
00:01:40.325 --> 00:01:44.770
The goats came out of their shelter, and
the cold began to fade.

23
00:01:46.085 --> 00:01:52.590
From that day on, Dácil told the story
whenever the volcano seemed to be waking.

24
00:01:53.105 --> 00:01:59.705
And when she finished, every voice
repeated: “Achamán, bring back Magec and

25
00:01:59.705 --> 00:02:01.230
bring back the light.”

